{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Ms. ___ . I’m Dr. ___ , one of the surgical team. You were admitted because of ongoing pain and circulation issues in your left hand related to your dialysis access graft. Do you remember discussing this with your surgeon before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I had that graft placed a while back. It caused hand pain—like coldness, numbness. I was told it might be stealing blood flow. But I didn’t want it removed at the time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. That’s called ‘steal syndrome.’ Your symptoms didn’t get worse, so you kept using it for dialysis. But now there are new ulcers on your left hand, and your right hand is also having circulation problems. We think it’s safer to remove the graft now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So you’re going to take it out? But how will I get dialysis then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do the graft removal today. After that, a temporary dialysis catheter will be placed in your neck so you can continue dialysis safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… I’m nervous about the surgery. Is it risky with my heart and diabetes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve reviewed your history—your heart function is stable, and your blood work is within acceptable limits. The surgery is relatively straightforward. We’ll monitor you closely. Your blood pressure and blood sugar will be checked often."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. And my hand—will it get better after the graft is gone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hope so. Removing the graft should improve blood flow to your hand. But we also saw that your arteries are quite calcified, which makes circulation difficult. We’ll get a CT scan today to see exactly what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had so many scans. Will this one show why my fingers keep cracking and forming scabs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the CT will show the blood vessels in your arms and hands. If there’s poor flow due to blockages, that could explain the ulcers and fissures. We may need to see a hand surgeon later for possible revascularization."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Revascularization? What does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2171-04-22 06:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It means trying to restore blood flow through surgery or a procedure, like opening up narrowed arteries. But we’ll know more after the scan. For now, focus on getting through today’s surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The surgery went well. We successfully ligated the graft in your left arm. You tolerated it without any issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My arm feels heavy, but no sharp pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There might be some swelling or bruising. We saw a small hematoma under the dressing, but it’s not concerning. You’ll have a new dialysis line placed tomorrow morning so you can dialyze safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why not today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We wanted to make sure you were stable after surgery. The procedure to place the line requires imaging guidance and a radiology team, which is scheduled for tomorrow at 12 p.m."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And the CT scan—did it show anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. The larger arteries up to your elbow are open, but the smaller ones in your forearms and hands are heavily calcified. We can’t tell if blood is flowing through them on this type of scan. The hand surgeon reviewed it and thinks you might benefit from a more detailed test later—maybe an MRA."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So my hands won’t heal unless they fix the blood flow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s part of it. Your diabetes and kidney disease also slow healing. But improving circulation could help prevent more ulcers. The hand surgeon will see you as an outpatient to discuss options."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I already lost part of my leg. I don’t want to lose fingers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2171-04-22 12:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. That’s why we’re acting now. The graft was likely making things worse. Removing it was the right step. We’ll do everything we can to preserve your hand function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2171-04-23 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today we’ll place your dialysis catheter in the left side of your neck. It’ll go into the jugular vein and reach your heart. You’ll be given some sedation, and the radiologist will use ultrasound and X-ray to guide it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2171-04-23 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2171-04-23 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll feel some pressure and numbing shots, but the sedation will help you relax. Most patients tolerate it well. Afterward, you’ll get dialysis through it, and we’ll make sure it’s working before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—your dialysis catheter was placed successfully. The tip is in the right atrium, and both ports are flowing well. You just finished your dialysis session and did fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t feel much. Just sleepy. Is the catheter permanent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This one is temporary. Since your left arm graft is gone, your team will decide if you need a new access—maybe in your right arm or leg. That’ll be discussed at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if everything stays stable. Your hand pain is no worse, you’re eating, and you’ve done dialysis safely through the new line. We’ll send you home with instructions and a follow-up appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call us if you develop fever, redness or pus at the incision or catheter site, chest pain, shortness of breath, or if your hand pain worsens. Also, monitor your weight—call if you gain more than 3 pounds in a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue all your usual medicines—insulin, blood pressure pills, aspirin, apixaban, and the others. We’ve sent the updated list to your pharmacy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I take tramadol for pain. Is that okay with the other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but take it only as needed. Avoid driving while on it. And don’t take extra acetaminophen—stick to the prescribed dose to protect your liver."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the hand surgeon appointment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re scheduled for next week. They’ll evaluate whether you’re a candidate for a procedure to improve blood flow to your hands. It’s important to keep that visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be there. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2171-04-23 13:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. A nurse will go over wound care and how to keep the catheter site clean. You’re doing well—just keep following up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2171-04-23 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your CT also showed gallstones and a small cyst in your pancreas. Nothing urgent, but your primary doctor should follow up on those with an MRI later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2171-04-23 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "More tests? I’m tired of being poked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2171-04-23 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. But this is just monitoring. The cyst is likely benign, but we want to make sure it doesn’t change. Your doctor will coordinate it when you’re ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2171-04-23 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. As long as it’s not surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2171-04-23 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No surgery planned. Focus on healing your hands and staying on track with dialysis and diabetes care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2171-04-23 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2171-04-23 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll have your wheelchair ready shortly, and a nurse will go over your discharge instructions one more time before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2171-04-23 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready to go home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2171-04-22 05:53:00",
